WEBVTT

00:01:28.035 --> 00:01:30.924
(Music)

00:01:30.948 --> 00:01:33.146
(Applause)

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.321
Thank you.

00:01:34.345 --> 00:01:35.693
Good evening and welcome to:

00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:38.705
"Spot the TED Presenter Who Used
to Be a Broadway Accompanist."

00:01:38.729 --> 00:01:39.867
(Laughter)

00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:43.406
When I was offered the Times
column six years ago,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.638
the deal was like this:

00:01:44.662 --> 00:01:48.041
you'll be sent the coolest, hottest,
slickest new gadgets.

00:01:48.065 --> 00:01:49.976
Every week, it'll arrive at your door.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.653
You get to try them out,
play with them, evaluate them

00:01:52.677 --> 00:01:55.749
until the novelty wears out,
before you have to send them back,

00:01:55.773 --> 00:01:57.100
and you'll get paid for it.

00:01:57.124 --> 00:01:59.622
You can think about it, if you want.

00:01:59.646 --> 00:02:04.271
So, I've always been a technology nut,
and I absolutely love it.